            "review_title": "Review at Highlands Coffee",
            "review_text": "Brooke H\n2 contributions\n0\nExpensive Instant Coffee\nJun 2019 • Couples\nI'm not sure if this is the right location of Highlands Coffee. When I went to one, it was fabulous. The next time, it was a waste of about 150,000 Dong and a really bad experience.\n\nThe staff randomly gave us large Cappuccinos even though we asked for small. One thing I don't like is being in a cafe and being handed paper cups, especially when it's not Starbucks. We asked to switch, they literally took two empty cups and slammed them on our tray and told us to change it ourselves.\n\nThen we taste the coffee... it was definitely either Nescafe or instant. Powder and all. It was one of the worst tasting cappuccino's I've ever had in my life. (No joke). And, if you are an avid coffee lover like me, then you know exactly what the difference in the two tastes like.\n\nWhen we asked them to remake it properly, they refused and said it was a cappuccino and they wouldn't do anything about it. \n\nIn the end, there was no Cappuccino and the group of kids that were working there started laughing at the circumstances as we walked out the door. \n\nConsidering it's Vietnam and there's supposed to pride in coffee making, go down the street to the local cafes instead. You'll find a much more pleasant attitude, cheaper price and you will actually get real coffee.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten June 7, 2019",
