            "review_title": "Review at Highlands Coffee",
            "review_text": "silvercode\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam229 contributions\n0\nGood coffee. Much better than Starbucks. And less expensive.\nNov 2017 • Family\nAfter the traditional meal “nem nuong Ninh Hoa”, in the rain we took a taxi to Highland Coffee, surprisingly the Vietnamese ice coffee and condensed milk was rather good and it beat Starbucks in many ways. I am in Vietnam and like the authentic food and drinks. This is a modern place that will accommodate any customer from all over the world. I am so proud after years of trying to be good, Highland have done it.\nIf you are a foreigner visiting Vietnam, please feel free to give this place a try. Nice atmosphere, clean, safe and you can sit by the windows to view the street.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten November 11, 2017",
